 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "bubbles is an m x n matrix of positive colors. One round: a bubble explodes when at least two of its orthogonal neighbours have its color; it explodes together with those same-colored neighbours. All explosions of a round happen at once and leave empty cells (0). Then, in every column, the remaining bubbles fall down to fill the empty cells, keeping their order, so empty cells collect at the top. Rounds repeat until a round has no explosion. Return the final matrix as a new matrix.",
  "provenance": [
